        "original_id": "63ceda27-ad9e-52c5-8d92-ddff854673af",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Sidney Herbert Sime, Lord Dunsany, Queen Victoria\n- Roles: English artist, Irish author\n- Places: United Kingdom\n- Periods: Victorian era\n- Topics: fantastic art, satirical art, story illustration\n\nFacts:\n- The Victorian era in the history of the United Kingdom was the period of Queen Victoria's reign from 20 June 1837 to 22 January 1901.\n- Sidney Herbert Sime was born in 1865 and died on 22 May 1941.\n- Sidney Herbert Sime, often called S. H. Sime, was an English artist active in the late Victorian and succeeding periods.\n- Sidney Herbert Sime is mostly remembered for fantastic and satirical artwork.\n- Sidney Herbert Sime was especially known for illustrating stories by the Irish author Lord Dunsany.",
